6) How to use this software: Start-up and Basic Commands

   6.1) Preparation

      As the preprocessing of the software, we first use Brill's
      tagger to assign a lexical category to each word in the
      analyzed sentence. This procedure is described in 
      'src/R-LRParser/README'. A simple example is shown as follows.

      1) Let "sfile" be a file including the sentences we would like
         to analyze. Then type

         %  src/R-LRParser/runtagger sfile 

         As the result, a file named "sfile.re" is created. In this
         file, each sentence in "sfile" is tagged with a lexical
         category and the output is in the form of prolog clause.

      2) Create a symbolic link from "sfile.re" to "sent_file.re".

   6.2) Start Up

      In this software, a LR table will be constructed from a context
      free grammar. And then, from this table, a set of prolog clauses
      corresponding to the items in the table is generated. These
      clauses and the "main program" of R-LRPar are formed LR parser.

      The series of this procedure is almost executed automatically.
      Such method is shown as follows. Here, the current directory is
      "src/LR_prolog".

      1) Start up a prolog interpreter. (under src/LR_prolog)

      2) Type "[run]." to read in "run.pl" into prolog database.

      3) Type "start." to start up the parser．In each step, 
         a help menu is provided.

   6.3) Basic Commands

   ・ "start." for executing the parser, R-LRPar
   ・ h        for help
   ・ c        for changing the set of analyzed sentences
   ・ l        for displaying the set of sentences
   ・ l(N,M)   for displaying N-th to M-th sentences
   ・ N        (an integer) for analyzing N-th sentence
   ・ q        for exit

   6.4) An Example

      The following is the sample execution of the parser under the
      directory named "src/LR_prolog".

---------- Begin Example (1) ----------
SICStus 3  #3: Wed Apr 17 01:11:05 JST 1996
| ?- [run].
{consulting ~/work/project/icot/Software/src/LR_prolog/run.pl...}
{consulting ~/work/project/icot/Software/src/LR_prolog/mymakegss.pl...}
..........         ..........
..........         ..........
..........         ..........
{~/work/project/icot/Software/src/LR_prolog/start.pl consulted, 3520 msec 145104 bytes}

****************************************
*  Type "start." to start the process  *
****************************************

{~/work/project/icot/Software/src/LR_prolog/run.pl consulted, 205250 msec 3944288 bytes}

yes
| ?- 
---------- End Example (1) ----------
The above is the execution of "run.pl" under a prolog interpreter.
Note that there are several files read into the prolog database.
---------- explantion (1) ----------

=====================================================================

