7) A Brief Guidance

    o How to use the software
  
        1) Type " prolog " to start up prolog interpreter.
        2) Type " ['src/LR_prolog/run']. " to consult the system.
        3) Type "start." to start up the system.
        4) Type "h." to see the help menu.
        5) Type the item we want in the help menu

    o How to change the set of sentences

        1) Let "sfile" be the name of the file including the sentences
           you want to analyze. Then type the following command at shell.

           %  src/R-LRParser/runtagger sfile 

           As the result, "sfile.re" is generated.

        2) Put a symbolic link from "sfile.re" to "sent_file.re" by 
           typing the following commands.

           % /bin/rm src/LR_prolog/sent_file.re
           % ln -s sfile src/LR_prolog/sent_file.re

        3) Type '[changesent].' on prolog interpreter to change the
           set of sentences.

